{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanQuark","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanQuark","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.VecNotation"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.baryon_mass_from_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.baryon_mass_from_volume","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorromeanQuark.lean#L69-L104","doc":"**The mass calibration, stated as an identity rather than as a\ndischarged hypothesis** (bean `qou-znut`, resolved 2026-08-24).\n\nThis was a `class BorromeanQuark` with a `topological_mass : ℝ → ℝ`\nfield and a `volume_calibrates_mass` field asserting that field\nequals `borromean_volume / (1 - 1/q)²`, plus an unguarded\n`instance canonical` supplying the right-hand side as the field's\nvalue so the assertion closed by `rfl`.\n\nThe reading recorded here is that this is **definitional and that is\ncorrect**: `topological_mass` never was an independent functional\nthat had to be shown to agree with a volume formula. It *is* the\nvolume formula. The instance's docstring said so — \"the\nmass-calibration identity holds definitionally\" — and the class\ndocstring already conceded the part that is genuinely open, that\nexhibiting a Borromean configuration \"does not establish that the\nphysical nucleon is one\" and that identification \"stays an **open**\nconjectural interpretation in the narrative\".\n\nWhat the typeclass added was the appearance of a hypothesis. A\nreader meeting `theorem baryon_mass_from_volume [BorromeanQuark]`\ntakes it for a derivation of baryon mass from hyperbolic volume,\ndischarged by an instance; it is a rewriting of a definition, and\n`baryon_mass` below was already that definition. Since the reading\nis that there was nothing to discharge, the honest shape is the one\nwithout the binder — a `def` and a `theorem … := rfl`. Dropping the\nclass changes no proof: `baryon_mass_from_volume`'s content is\nunchanged, and it now says as much in its type.\n\n**What is NOT claimed here, and was not claimed before.** That the\nphysical nucleon mass is `borromean_volume / (1 - 1/q)²`. That is\n`conj:borromean-quark`, it lives in the narrative, and no Lean\ndeclaration in this file asserts it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.baryon_mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.baryon_mass","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorromeanQuark.lean#L62-L65","doc":"The baryon mass from the topological mass formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.borromean_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.borromean_volume","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorromeanQuark.lean#L58-L60","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the Borromean complement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.neutron_partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.neutron_partition","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorromeanQuark.lean#L49-L56","doc":"The neutron: one up (+1) and two down (-1), net charge 0.\nColor assignment: one quark per color tube (bijective). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.proton_partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.proton_partition","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorromeanQuark.lean#L40-L47","doc":"The proton: two up (+1) and one down (-1), net charge +1.\nColor assignment: one quark per color tube (bijective). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon.charge_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon.charge_sum","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorromeanQuark.lean#L38-L38","doc":"The orientations sum to the net Coulomb charge ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon.orientation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon.orientation","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorromeanQuark.lean#L36-L36","doc":"Crossing orientation: +1 (up) or -1 (down) for each component ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon.color","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon.color","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorromeanQuark.lean#L34-L34","doc":"The three color tube assignments ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon.mk","kind":"ctor","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorromeanQuark.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanBaryon","kind":"structure","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BorromeanQuark.lean#L31-L38","doc":"The Borromean link of three unknots in color tubes. ","signatureChunk":0}]}